    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Neaff4fa2a96245a5937a7e18cfea120e"/>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>The package implements methods to compare lists of genes based on comparing the corresponding 'functional profiles'.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <obo:IAO_0000119>http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.4/bioc/html/goProfiles.html</obo:IAO_0000119>
    <dcterms:creator>Nandini Badarinarayan</dcterms:creator>
    <rdfs:label>goProfiles</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SWO_1100003">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000064"/>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>The ACME algorithm is quite straightforward. Using a user-dened quantile of the data,called the threshold, any probes in the data that are above that threshold are considered positive probes. A p-value is then assigned to each probe.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <rdfs:label>'ACME'</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
