  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SWO_0000669">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SWO_0000001"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Nec4bb7480cf14187805713192a3d8223"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N19c33810e80747b4a6b37ef546ecd7a4"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Ne494fa741814449c81a3a678156689f8"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N9d48d750ae4b4168b55d8adfd223c612"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Nc2eacdd7b6914d1180c3410e8c7c103d"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N876d58fd63034549ba7290335e865c13"/>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Most analyses of Affymetrix GeneChip data are based on point estimates of expression levels and ignore the uncertainty of such estimates. By propagating uncertainty to downstream analyses we can improve results from microarray analyses. For the first time, the puma package makes a suite of uncertainty propagation methods available to a general audience. puma also offers improvements in terms of scope and speed of execution over previously available uncertainty propagation methods.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <obo:IAO_0000119>http://bioconductor.org/packages/2.4/bioc/html/puma.html</obo:IAO_0000119>
    <dcterms:creator>Nandini Badarinarayan</dcterms:creator>
    <rdfs:label>puma</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
