    <obo:IAO_0000115>The UMLS Metathesaurus License is a vendor-specific license which allows redistribution (as part of a larger computer application) as long as the original data is attributed correctly and a summary of data use provided each year. There is no cost to use the service, and may be used both commercially and non-commercially. Users must inform the resource if it is redistributed within a computer application.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <obo:IAO_0000119>https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/license.html, accessed 13 July 2016.</obo:IAO_0000119>
    <dcterms:creator>Allyson Lister</dcterms:creator>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">UMLS Metathesaurus License</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SWO_1100064">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SWO_0000001"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N82d1b7bbae3045f79301598da129ff5a"/>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Versarray ChipReader systems are highly sensitive laser confocal systems designed for rapid imaging of microarrays. These are advanced scanners that meet your expectations, differentiating between a spot response and background level, and optimizing the signal on the bottom as well as the top end of the range for increased sensitivity. Results with versarray chipreader systems have a low background, enhanced weak signal detection, and virtually no photobleaching for a long dye lifetime.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <obo:IAO_0000118>VersArray ChipReader</obo:IAO_0000118>
    <obo:IAO_0000119>http://www.bio-medicine.org/</obo:IAO_0000119>
    <dcterms:creator>Nandini Badarinarayan</dcterms:creator>
    <rdfs:label>ChipReader 3.1</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
