    <obo:IAO_0000115>In mathematics, an ordinary differential equation or ODE is an equation containing a function of one independent variable and its derivatives. The term "ordinary" is used in contrast with the term partial differential equation which may be with respect to more than one independent variable.</obo:IAO_0000115>
