  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SWO_3000070">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SWO_3000069"/>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>Tabix indexes a TAB-delimited genome position file and creates an index file when region is absent from the command-line. The input data file must be position sorted and compressed by bgzip which has a gzip like interface. After indexing, tabix is able to quickly retrieve data lines overlapping regions specified in the format "chr:beginPos-endPos". Fast data retrieval also works over network if URI is given as a file name and in this case the index file will be downloaded if it is not present locally.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <obo:IAO_0000119>http://samtools.sourceforge.net/tabix.shtml</obo:IAO_0000119>
    <rdfs:label>tabix file format</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
